# App portfolio face

The portfolio is a **one-page public face**, not a Portal action dashboard.

## Face contents

- Identity (avatar, name, **full** NEAR account id as handle, full bio)
- Connected visitor gestures under bio: **Stand · Endorse · Support** (quiet text + colored arrows; no pills)
- Signals (standing · solidarity · endorsements · reputation) — browse metrics
- Links
- Dock (connect / account / summon)

## Page drawer (Launch)

Owner-customizable scroll surface — **extension of the face**, not a second portfolio:

- Tall glass sheet (~95dvh) so a thin strip of mood face stays visible
- Compact header: **name** + one facts line (`N posts · N guilds · Joined Mon YYYY ›`) + jump chips; DAO roles / tags live in the Joined account-facts sheet
- **Joined** is clickable → slim account-facts sheet (Portal-style), not a second face card
- Account facts OnSocial: Joined · fused `Updated Mar 12 · Name · Banner` (omit when same day as Joined) · activity/roles/tags when present; NEAR: Network · Account · Created
- Drawer body is a **curated portfolio**: peek sections → See all; hide empty sections
- Jump chips live in **header chrome** under facts (not in the scroll body); scroll-spy active state; compact chips; mood tint on **active chip only**; smooth-scroll to sections
- Default order: posts → guilds → collectibles → links → badges
- One sheet-body scroller; overlay footer pill (**Stand · Endorse · Support**) absolutely on the panel (`height: auto`, not in flex flow); content scrolls under it; launcher hide on scroll down / reveal on scroll up or top; jump briefly tucks the pill; connect whisper when disconnected; hidden for self
- Support is **not** a drawer section — gestures only
- Dock arrows match Stand size (`0.55rem`), not the larger face signal clamp
- Face keeps link **icons**; drawer Links shows label + hostname / handle rows
- No avatar / `@id` / bio — face already owns those
- No reputation band names — score/rank stay on the face
- Mood-thread chrome + thin drag grip; sections scroll inside
- Hide zero counts

## Mood

Page mood is **identity chrome** for the portfolio face and any surface that should feel like “this person’s page / this viewer’s wallet.” Reuse the same stack — do not invent a second mood system.

### Visitor vs owner

| Surface | Whose mood |
|---------|------------|
| Face / portfolio wash / Launch (page) drawer | **Page** (`effectiveMood` on `portfolio-os-layer`) |
| Summon dock / grip / pill (`portfolio-summon-dock`) | **Viewer** everywhere (`useViewerDockMood` via `AppShellLauncher` / visit path); **owner** uses live `effectiveMood` so mood preview paints the dock |
| OS app screens / slide-overs (`OsAppScreen`, `OsSlideOverScreen`) | **Viewer** by default (`useViewerDockMood`); `moodId={null}` keeps blue-corner trial; pass explicit mood only for rare overrides |
| Create-post / wallet sheets | **Viewer** (`useViewerWalletMoodVars` / dock hook) |

**Host (page) mood stays on the portfolio face only** — Launch drawer + face gesture sheets. Guild / hub / collection / drop shells use **viewer** mood when logged in (or none logged out). Do not retint those shells with the page owner’s mood.

**Typing fields on mood surfaces** use `os-field-bordered` (transparent fill + lip so wash shows through). Reserve `os-field-soft` for quiet non-mood OS sheets (e.g. dense hug sheets without host/viewer wash).

Do **not** paint the whole `portfolio-os-layer` with viewer mood when visiting — only the dock. Finish-specific summon CSS targets `.portfolio-summon-dock[data-mood=…]`, not the os-layer.

### Source of truth

- Resolve via `@/lib/moods/resolve` (`resolvePortfolioMood`, `resolvePortfolioMoodForPreview`, `portfolioMoodShellStyle`)
- Live face: `PortfolioShellRoot` + `PortfolioMoodPreviewProvider` (`effectiveMood`)
- Viewer wallet mood elsewhere: `useViewerWalletMoodVars` (seed with protocol fallback so sheets don’t flash blue-corner trial)
- Viewer dock chrome (all OS screens + visiting): `useViewerDockMood` on `.portfolio-summon-dock`
- Page-owner mood on *their* sheets: portfolio `mood` / page mood hooks — not a hard-coded accent
- Owner portfolio dock: `effectiveMood` (preview-aware) on `.portfolio-summon-dock`

### Intensity (must match)

Portfolio wash mixes — **same on picker cards, live shell, home, and create-post**:

| Token | Dark | Light |
|-------|------|-------|
| `--mood-bg-preset-mix` | `25%` | `30%` |
| `--mood-text-preset-mix` | `18%` | `18%` |
| `--mood-muted-preset-mix` | `18%` | `18%` |

Light bumps bg mix so the wash reads closer to dark (light presets are subtler on white). Title uses the mood accent (Gold keeps foil); tagline stays muted. Row type stays compact — do not inherit portfolio face name scale / ornaments.

### Reuse on posts / slide-overs / sheets

`OsAppScreen` / `OsSlideOverScreen` apply connected viewer mood by default — do not re-thread `moodId`/`moodStyle` on every panel.

When a surface should carry mood outside those shells (compose post, manage flows, account sheets):

1. Resolve mood → CSS vars (`portfolioMoodShellStyle` / viewer hook `style`)
2. Pass **`moodId` + `moodStyle`** into the shell (`OsSlideOverScreen`, glass sheet, or portfolio panel) — or omit and let `OsAppScreen` / `OsSlideOverScreen` default
3. Prefer subtle `--mood-bg` under translucent glass — do not rely on opaque glass that hides the wash
4. `moodId={null}` only when blue-corner trial is intentional
5. Compose / slide-over: even `--mood-bg` only inside the app column (phone view); desktop gutters stay OS `--bg` (black / white) — **no outside mood glow** (portfolio desktop hairline only, no `0 0 20px` accent halo; slide-over clears card radius so host glow can’t bleed)

Reference: create-post (`guild-composer-sheet`) may still pass viewer mood explicitly; most app routes inherit from `OsAppScreen`.

### Save / preview (customize mood)

- Preview while browsing; on successful chain save call **`commitMoodPreview(moodId)`** — do not `discardMoodPreview()` (avoids snap-back to stale SSR)
- After apply: `seedViewerCommittedMood` + wallet `setMood` + `router.refresh()`
- Shell prefers live RSC `mood`/`config` props; soft-fill from chain only when SSR config was empty
- Toast / button contract: see `app-button-toast-contract.mdc` (preview bar + mood save)

### Do not (mood)

- Different mix % on cards vs portfolio
- Per-button or one-off mood color hacks outside resolve + CSS vars
- Clear preview on save before props catch up (use commit)
- Assume hard refresh is required for mood to stick

## Gesture row

| Control | Arrow hue | Behavior |
|---------|-----------|----------|
| **Stand** / Standing / Step back | `--signal-standing` | Inline toggle (ledger + dots; Step back on hover) |
| **Endorse** | `--signal-endorse` | Opens endorsements overlay (compose there) |
| **Support** | `--signal-reputation` | Opens dedicated Support glass sheet |

Even trio with · separators. Same control height as standing modal; **no border**; hover = soft bg wash.

## Before vs after connect

| State | Face |
|-------|------|
| Disconnected | Full face + dock connect only — **no** gesture row |
| Connected visitor | Same face + Stand · Endorse · Support under bio |
| Owner / self | No visitor gestures; when unclaimed target balance > 0: **gift · amount · Collect** in the same slot |

## Off-face depth

- **Standing lists** — signal taps → standing overlay
- **Endorsements** — endorse signal / face Endorse → endorsements overlay + compose sheet
- **Support** — face Support + drawer Stand · Support whisper → dedicated `ProfileSupportSheet` (amount + `trackTransaction`)
  - Form stack: amount → presets left / available right → outcome → CTA
  - Outcome line **live only** from `get_action_config` — never show hardcoded % fallback
  - Valid amount morphs same line to SOCIAL amounts (`0.99 to them · 0.01 protocol boost`)
  - While loading: `Loading split…`; on failure: soft error + Retry; Support gated until live + active
  - Say **protocol boost**, not treasury
  - **Received support (owner):** face Collect line (`PortfolioOwnerSupportCollect`) — gift icon + amount + Collect; claims shared `get_target_balance` pot (profile support, endorsement support, boost-post author share); `claim_target_balance` + `trackTransaction`; owner-only; hide when zero; not in account sheet

## Gesture sheet chrome (Support / Endorse compose)

`OsGestureSheet` from `@onsocial/ui` — hug glass + `GestureSheetHeader` over the portfolio face (mood peek). **Not** a post-compose slide-over. Same family for Support, Endorse, scarce buy/sell, protocol tasks:

- **Host mood** — page owner (`mood` prop or `usePageOwnerMood`); signal hues via `supportSheetPanelStyle` into `panelStyle`
- **Typing fields** — `os-field-bordered` so wash shows through
- One title beat — **not** a duplicate face-card strip
- Fused title: signal-colored verb + person (`Support Voter 02`, `Endorse …`)
- Quiet `@` + **full account id** under the title (never strip `.near` / `.testnet`)
- Optional one-line whisper only when relationship state exists
- Close control top-right

Do not hand-roll `GlassSheet` + `GestureSheetHeader` for this family. Amount / suffix type-ins: `AmountField` / `SuffixField` from `@onsocial/ui`. Presets / Max / balance: `AmountFieldMetaRow`. Account type-in chrome: `OsAccountField` (app `NearAccountField` wraps sanitize + probe). Soft-egg −/value/+ qty: `CollectionQtyStepper`. Unit marks: `TokenIcon`.

Shared header primitive: `GestureSheetHeader`. Identity labels use `fallbackLabel` / raw `accountId` — full NEAR id.

## Do not

- Copy Portal’s bordered Support + Endorse + Stand pill cluster
- Show disabled action CTAs pre-connect
- Put the money Support **form** on the mood face or inline in the page drawer (sheet only)
- Open the page content drawer for face Support
- Use bordered pills on face gestures **or face tags**
- Put profile tags on the face — drawer only (quiet text, no pills)
- Re-introduce the person in the page drawer (no second avatar · name · handle card; no bio bridge)
- Stack avatar · name · handle **and** a bare verb title on gesture sheets when already on their face
- Open the page drawer as a full-bleed wipe — keep a mood-face peek
